{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/879231-how-to-play-a-ghost-blooded-solar-in-3e","id":879231,"title":"How to play a Ghost-Blooded Solar in 3e","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-30T21:03:59-07:00","id":879231,"title":"How to play a Ghost-Blooded Solar in 3e","content":"My 770xp Lunar has gone insane (well, more insane than he was before), and developed permanent mutations (again) so his daughter has (wisely) decided that it's finally time to take him to a No Moon elder for Silver Pact training and tattooing.<br /> <br /> So, I need to make a new character. This is a 2e game, but I think the ST would like to convert to 3rd ed later this year. So, I think it's probably easier to make a 3rd ed character and reverse-convert it to 2nd ed for now, rather than the other way round.<br /> <br /> I like to investigate stuff in games (my Lunar had most of the Perception tree, for tracking and so forth), so I'm thinking about investigation-based concepts.<br /> <br /> One idea I had was for a ghost-blooded investigator. Something like a Dhampyr: being the son of an undead creature gives him useful powers for fighting undead, or rather, investigating them (putting hauntings to rest by finding out about their unfinished business, for example), and also investigating murders (as he can interview ghosts with his ghost-related powers). Not an Abyssal: he doesn't champion the dead, he protects the living from the dead (well, the bad dead: he'll probably work with nice ghosts).<br /> <br /> So... how do I make a ghost-blooded Solar? I'd like the forum's advice.<br /> <br /> Option 1: He just uses all the regular rules for any other Solar, but has white hair and red eyes or something. And has various appropriate specialties. It'll do, but it's not very interesting..<br /> <br /> Option 2: Some kind of ridiculous mechanical disaster with arconoi and weird xp like 2e. Clearly a terrible idea.<br /> <br /> Option 3: I use powers that are available to Solars in the Corebook to represent his ghosty powers. For example, he could be an Eclipse, and have the two ghost charms that are available to Eclipses (cursing someone with nightmares and creating a cloud of darkness only the dead can see through) to represent powers he inherited. I think Night fits a little better, but Eclipse is okay. I could give him the thaumaturgical ritual to banish ghosts. He could take the hearthstone that lets you speak to ghosts at their graves I guess, though it also lets everyone else in three miles do it too, which doesn't fit so well. Can anyone think of other powers in the Core that Solars could take which I could refluff as powers he has for being a ghost-blooded? Charms, merits, evocations, sorcerous initiation merits, etc?<br /> <br /> Option 4: I make up some supernatural merits to represent his ghost-blooded nature (if the ST approves of them). But what? I'd like to give him the ability to see ghosts, but not demons or other dematerialised spirits. Just ghosts. Or perhaps he should be able to see and touch ghosts, but they can see and touch him, like someone who's beent taking loads of Ghost Flower Tea. What rating do you think that would be?<br /> Can you think of any other merits that would make sense for a ghost-blooded?<br /> I'll probably want to convert Summon Ghost as well (should be easy enough, based on Summon Demon) and maybe a couple of other necromantic spells, too.<br /> <br /> Option 5: Basically option 4, but not so egregrious. I make up a necromantic initiation to represent being a ghost-blooded, and as most initiations have 1 or 2 merits, that comes with some appropriate merits. Or I do it with Thaumaturgy.<br /> <br /> <br /> I should say that I'm more interested in the flavour of a ghost-blood who protects the living than in having powerful powers of cheesiness. Hence why I'd be willing to go with 1, I just think it's dull.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 05-01-2016, 12:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T21:27:33-07:00","id":879250,"title":"","content":"I do not know if that would work, the UC does not like to share his toys. That being said, the strange abilities could be modeled by the thaumaturgy merit, with each being a supernatural merit that costs four points to take and one point of Willpower to use for a turn. Sorcery workings can do the rest probably.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T21:41:28-07:00","id":879258,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11683\" data-vbnamecard=\"11683\">Aya Tari</a> - I think the Sun can and will make ANY human that He judges worthy into a Solar, be they normal human, or some kind of Godblood. If they're not some other kind of Exalt, they're eligible to become a Solar.<br /> <br /> Anyway, you might want to go with like Option 4 or 5. See if any Supernatural Merits fit your concept. Maybe you could take Influence 1 with relation to known among many of the ghosts as a wandering Necromancer.<br /> <br /> See if you can purchase the Tempered by the Elements (2-dot) Merit in relation to surviving in the Shadowlands, or other places of Death.<br /> <br /> And there's a 2-dot Merit called Unburnt Majesty, which gives you a bonus against fire attacks. Maybe you could adapt a Merit that lets your Ghost Blood gain a resistance against the life-draining touch of several types of undead?<br /> <br /> The ability to see Ghosts might be a 4-dot Merit, considering that a Keen Mortal Sense is 3-dots.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T21:57:09-07:00","id":879270,"title":"","content":"I wonder if we will get any other skill enhancing merits... The Keen Sense Merit is just a double specialty of Alertness, with a minor disadvantage associated with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T22:05:10-07:00","id":879276,"title":"","content":"I'd go with any of those options, excepting #2 that is. #3 seems best, especially with the Eclipse power and the ability of Eclipses to take Occult.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T22:31:43-07:00","id":879294,"title":"","content":"Of course, 4 and 5 are the most sensible.<br /> <br /> Just a couple of unique merits that you take at character gen to represent that portion of your blood.<br /> <br /> Eyes of the Ancestor: Cost: 2<br /> Death sees you as one of its own, and you see it back. This merit allows you to always be able to sense nearby ghosts, and even see them as a hazy outline if they are immaterial. With a small effort, you can shift your vision to see them fully. Pay 1 willpower in order to see immaterial ghosts for the remainder of the scene.<br /> <br /> Grasp of Dead Hands: Cost: 3<br /> The dead shiver when you walk over their graves. This merit allows you to spend a willpower in order to affect unwilling ghosts as if they were manifest for the remainder of the scene, even if they are immaterial. If a ghost wishes it, however, you can effect them for no cost.<br /> <br /> The Last Breath: Cost: 5<br /> Death runs thick in your veins and hangs on to your spirit, seeming to rot your very soul. Being that much closer to death, you can feel and affect the death of others. Should you be nearby a dying, and willing, individual, you can ensure that they become a ghost upon death, and not pass on to Lethe. Should they agree, you gain Temporary Willpower equal to your Willpower, which can exceed your maximum rating, and they rise again as a ghost the next time the sun sets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/697-arteliex","name":"Arteliex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar697_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T23:13:41-07:00","id":879315,"title":"","content":"Thanks guys, there's some good points here.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">That being said, the strange abilities could be modeled by the thaumaturgy merit, with each being a supernatural merit that costs four points to take and one point of Willpower to use for a turn.</div> </div> </div> </div>The cost doesn't matter a lot, since I can just take the Occult charm to get 4 thaumaturgical rituals.<br /> But yeah, that's how the thaumaturgist's ritual in the book works: &quot;As long as the exorcist is armed with her silver-inlaid staff and bracers, she may pay a point of Willpower to make them capable of striking dematerialized ghosts for one action. She still suffers a -3 penalty on attacks if targeting a ghost she cannot see.&quot;<br /> But then, hitting ghosts isn't really an issue with Occult charms. I mean, I could take it for the flavour, but I'd likely never use it when I could use spirit-cutting attack for 1m (although this does make me think that Occult charms can represent some of his powers anyway. How come he can hit spirits? Because he's ghost-blooded).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/879231-how-to-play-a-ghost-blooded-solar-in-3e?p=879250#post879250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorcery workings can do the rest probably.</div> </div> </div> </div>My first thought was &quot;oh, I can just add appropriate abilities to myself with sorcerous workings&quot; (well, necromantic workings, which probably just work the same way but more death-y), but I'd rather start with them to represent powers he's had from birth. Seems a bit strange for him to go meditate for a month and come back with a power he inherited from his parents (I guess you could argue he's &quot;unlocked&quot; them, but it's a little odd).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">See if any Supernatural Merits fit your concept. Maybe you could take Influence 1 with relation to known among many of the ghosts as a wandering Necromancer.</div> </div> </div> </div>There wasn't any supernatural merits in the book I felt fitted (except Thaumaturgist I guess), but Influence isn't a bad idea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">See if you can purchase the Tempered by the Elements (2-dot) Merit in relation to surviving in the Shadowlands, or other places of Death.<br /> <br /> And there's a 2-dot Merit called Unburnt Majesty, which gives you a bonus against fire attacks. Maybe you could adapt a Merit that lets your Ghost Blood gain a resistance against the life-draining touch of several types of undead?<br /> <br /> The ability to see Ghosts might be a 4-dot Merit, considering that a Keen Mortal Sense is 3-dots.</div> </div> </div> </div>For bonuses against attacks, I was thinking I'd just give him a bunch of specialties. Resistance and Integrity of &quot;vs ghosts&quot; and Survival &quot;the Underworld&quot;. It's not a big bonus, but it'd represent it thematically and easily. I could try swapping around some merits though.<br /> <br /> Ghost-Flower Tea is Resources 3, so for having its effects permanently, 4 dots does seem about right.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd go with any of those options, excepting #2 that is.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we can all agree that the way 2nd ed did God-Bloods was not the best way.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}